I have this Rogue character that I can't figure out what to do next.
He's gotten up to level 16 (last three levels from wraiths).

There's been a real shortage of ?EA, so even though he's got decent
armor and three points of priestly protection, he's only at -6.  Or I
should say was at -6 -- he got to the Castle level, and even though he
has no way of getting into the main castle area (no musical
instrument, no wand of striking), he has water walking boots, and
using the one potion of levitation he had, he managed to kill off the
four dragons and collect a set of grey dragon scales.  He's now
wearing those instead of the dwarf mithril mail, which gives him MR,
but brings the AC down to -3.

He can't do the quest, because he gets ambushed by nagas (and barely
escaped when he tried it).  He can't finish the castle because he
can't get in -- and isn't really buff enough to do it in any case.
What he _really_ needs is a magic marker to write a bunch of EA
scrolls, especially one to turn the scales into GDSM.  He does have a
ring of regeneration, which is a good portion of how he managed to
survive thus far.  

Any suggestions on what to do next, other than bumble around and hope
for the best?  I mostly run combat wombats, so this is new territory
to me.  (I am trying to run him as a proper rogue, with lots of
daggers from a distance, but I keep using up my supply and having to
go back to Stormbringer.)



